# docflow — LLM / VLM configuration template
#
#   cp .env.example .env        # then fill in what your deployment needs
#
# `.env` is ignored by git (see .gitignore); this template is committed on purpose.
#
# Two rules this file cannot bend:
#   * no default provider and no default model — an empty value is a missing
#     statement and stays a refusal, never a substituted stand-in;
#   * a credential is not an artifact field: the provider seam drops `api_key`
#     from the options it records, so it never lands in a run.
#
# The processor addresses two stages, each with its own provider, endpoint and
# credential. They are separate on purpose: a vision model and a text model are
# different services and must be swappable apart from each other.
#
# Accepted provider names (`docflow.llm.primitives.PROVIDER_KINDS`):
#   ollama | vllm | openai | openai_compatible
# `vllm`, `openai` and `openai_compatible` resolve to the same OpenAI-compatible
# transport; `ollama` has its own.
#
# What reads this file: the lab bench — `llm.py` and `batch_llm.py` — from the
# repository root, or from `$DOCFLOW_ENV_FILE` when a run keeps it elsewhere.
# The **library** does not read it, and must not: a request that meant one thing
# here and another where the file differs is the silent stand-in the processor
# refuses, so a caller of `docflow.llm` still states every value itself. A run
# that took anything from this file prints which keys, on its `config:` line.
#
# Precedence, narrowest first: a real environment variable, then this file, then
# the flag's own default. So `DOCFLOW_LLM_TIMEOUT=60 python scripts/tools/llm.py
# …` overrides the file, and `--option timeout=60` overrides both. A blank value
# is nothing stated rather than a value — it leaves the next source in charge.
#
# Read below: DOCFLOW_ASSETS_DIR, and the DOCFLOW_LLM_* transport, window,
# timeout and decoding settings. Deliberately NOT read:
#   * DOCFLOW_LLM_PROVIDER / DOCFLOW_LLM_MODEL — `--provider` and `--model` are
#     required flags on every inference subcommand, and a configuration file
#     must not be able to become a default model;
#   * the DOCFLOW_VLM_* block — the bench states one provider, one model and one
#     set of options per call, and a page call is the same call with an image
#     attached, so a second block would make the same flags mean two things
#     depending on the input's suffix. A vision model is still named with
#     `--model`; those names are for a library caller whose two stages really
#     are two services.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Text LLM — the extraction chain, over OCR text (`generate_text` and
# `generate_structured`, reached when the request names a schema)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Provider name. One of the four above. Blank is refused, not guessed.
DOCFLOW_LLM_PROVIDER=

# The model as that provider names it — Ollama `llama3.1`, vLLM's served id, or
# the hosted API's model id. Blank is refused, not guessed.
DOCFLOW_LLM_MODEL=

# Endpoint. Leave blank for the transport's documented local default, which is
# recorded in the run's metadata so it is never hidden:
#   ollama            -> http://localhost:11434
#   openai_compatible -> http://localhost:8000/v1
DOCFLOW_LLM_BASE_URL=

# Credential, sent as `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Blank for an
# unauthenticated local endpoint. Never recorded in an artifact.
DOCFLOW_LLM_API_KEY=

# Per-call timeout, in seconds. Blank uses the documented default of 30. A
# review that audits a reading carries the document, the proposal and the schema
# and reasons before it answers: 600 is what the registry's review step measured
# (302 s) with room to spare.
DOCFLOW_LLM_TIMEOUT=

# The model's context window, when the provider cannot state one. An
# OpenAI-compatible `/models` entry does not carry it, so this is the only way
# the processor can tell a prompt that does not fit from one that does. Since
# 2026-10-04 it is also the window the call asks for: the Ollama transport sends
# it as `num_ctx`. Leave it blank and the check cannot tell — which is not the
# same as "it fits", and is not reported as one.
DOCFLOW_LLM_CONTEXT_WINDOW=

# Ollama's own name for the same window, passed through to the daemon as `num_ctx`.
# It is a decoding option, so the processor's own check never reads it; prefer
# DOCFLOW_LLM_CONTEXT_WINDOW, which reaches the daemon *and* the check. If both
# are stated and disagree, DOCFLOW_LLM_CONTEXT_WINDOW wins — the transport
# replaces `num_ctx` with it, so the window that was checked is the window used.
# A reviewer that reasons before it answers needs the room either way — on
# Ollama's default window it runs out mid-thought and returns an EMPTY answer
# (`done_reason: length`). 16384 is what the registry's review step measured.
# It is Ollama's key: state it for a local `ollama` provider and leave it blank
# otherwise, since another transport receives it as an unknown body field.
DOCFLOW_LLM_NUM_CTX=

# Decoding options passed through to the provider. The seed is the determinism
# lever: without it, a run is not reproducible. `min_p` is the sampling floor —
# tokens below this probability are dropped before sampling, so a small value
# (0.05) trims the long tail a reasoning reviewer can wander into.
DOCFLOW_LLM_TEMPERATURE=
DOCFLOW_LLM_MIN_P=
DOCFLOW_LLM_SEED=

# Sampling parameters a model's card may name. deepseek-r1:8b publishes
# `temperature 0.6`, `top_p 0.95`, `repeat_penalty 1.0`, `presence_penalty 0.0`;
# leave them blank to keep the model's own defaults. `top_p` is the nucleus
# cutoff, and the two penalties fight repetition and loops.
DOCFLOW_LLM_TOP_P=
DOCFLOW_LLM_REPEAT_PENALTY=
DOCFLOW_LLM_PRESENCE_PENALTY=

# Ollama's thinking switch for a reasoning model — `true`/`false`, or a level
# (`low`/`medium`/`high`/`max`). `false` stops the model thinking before it
# answers, which is what keeps an 8B reviewer from looping; a model that does not
# think ignores it. It is a request field, not a model option: on Ollama the
# transport lifts it to the top of the `/api/chat` body, where the daemon reads
# it. Leave it blank for a transport that has no such switch.
DOCFLOW_LLM_THINK=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VLM — the multimodal reading of page images (`generate_multimodal`, reached
# when the request carries images)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Same four names as above. A vision model is a different model, so it gets its
# own provider, endpoint and credential rather than reusing the text ones.
DOCFLOW_VLM_PROVIDER=
DOCFLOW_VLM_MODEL=
DOCFLOW_VLM_BASE_URL=
DOCFLOW_VLM_API_KEY=
DOCFLOW_VLM_TIMEOUT=

# A vision model's window differs from the text model's; state it here.
DOCFLOW_VLM_CONTEXT_WINDOW=

DOCFLOW_VLM_TEMPERATURE=
DOCFLOW_VLM_SEED=

# Note: images and a schema on the same call are not modelled yet — for now the
# schema wins and the call is treated as structured text, so a VLM stage that
# must be validated uses the text path, or runs without a schema.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Assets — the template and schema registry the identifiers resolve against
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Layout the loader expects under this root:
#   <root>/template/<id>.md            prompt template
#   <root>/schema/<id>.schema.json     response schema
# An id may carry a sub-directory: `extraction/invoice` resolves to
# `<root>/template/extraction/invoice.md`. Nothing is guessed — a missing asset
# is a typed `DEPENDENCY_ERROR` naming the path it looked for.
DOCFLOW_ASSETS_DIR=registry

# `registry/` is the real registry and follows that layout exactly (see
# registry/README.md for the examples). `tests/fixtures/llm/` is the fixture
# root, and it is what the built-in chain's `simple_extract` / `simple` names
# resolve against — so `graph`, `fake` and `resume` need the fixtures, not this.
#
# This line is set in the template, so copying the file as it stands points the
# bench at the real registry. Leave it BLANK to keep `tests/fixtures/llm/` and
# the built-in chain working.
